215	<!-- 2 · The idea -->
216	<section class="scene" data-title="The idea" data-short="Idea">
217	  <div class="head">
218	    <p class="eyebrow">The idea</p>
219	    <h2>One Moneo. More screens.</h2>
220	    <p class="lede">Nothing runs on the phone. It shows the Moneo on your computer, so there is nothing to copy, sync or sign in to again.</p>
221	  </div>
222	  <div class="diagram" style="flex:none;width:1396px;height:500px">
223	    <div class="node" data-s="1" style="left:0;top:20px;width:290px;height:130px"><span class="pill">Laptop browser</span><h4>localhost:3000</h4><p>Exactly as it always was.</p></div>
224	    <div class="node" data-s="2" style="left:0;top:180px;width:290px;height:130px"><span class="pill p-brand">Phone</span><h4>Home-screen icon</h4><p>Opens your private address.</p></div>
225	    <div class="node" data-s="2" style="left:0;top:340px;width:290px;height:130px"><span class="pill p-brand">Tablet</span><h4>Home-screen icon</h4><p>Same address, and it can rotate.</p></div>
226	    <div class="node hl" data-s="3" style="left:480px;top:120px;width:380px;height:250px;background:var(--brand-soft)">
227	      <span class="pill p-brand">Your computer</span>
228	      <h4 style="font-size:26px">Moneo</h4>
229	      <p style="font-size:16px;margin-top:8px">Every page, question and sync runs here. A phone sends the same request a laptop tab would, and gets the same answer.</p>
230	    </div>
231	    <div class="node" data-s="4" style="left:1050px;top:20px;width:346px;height:130px"><span class="pill p-blue">On your computer</span><h4>Your database</h4><p>Postgres in Docker, never copied anywhere.</p></div>
232	    <div class="node ai" data-s="4" style="left:1050px;top:180px;width:346px;height:130px"><span class="pill p-ai">Already signed in</span><h4>ChatGPT or API key</h4><p>The phone uses the computer's sign-in.</p></div>
233	    <div class="node" data-s="4" style="left:1050px;top:340px;width:346px;height:130px"><span class="pill p-warn">Already connected</span><h4>Banks and Scalable</h4><p>Sync runs on the computer, from any screen.</p></div>
